
How can an offline mailbox fail without thread safety?
Offline Mailbox — Two people DM an offline user at the exact same time.
Both threads check "does Bob have a mailbox?" — he doesn't.
Both create a new list. One overwrites the other.
 A message is lost. This is a check-then-act race condition.

How did I make an offline mailbox safe?
To make the offline mailbox safe, we had to solve the check-then-act race condition.
One way we fixed it was by using computeIfAbsent, this ensures that only one thread creates
the queue and that all other threads get the same queue. This means that no overwriting occurs.
Another way we certified that our offline mailbox was thread safe was by using concurrent queues
and concurrent hash maps. The concurrent queue allows many threads to add messages without altering
the existing structure and the concurrent hashmaps allow for reads and writes without altering the map.